    "whyItMatters": "Relationship questions often appear as practical decisions rather than definition prompts. A client may like the counselor but reject the treatment goal; agree with the goal but not understand the intervention; or cooperate behaviorally while feeling unsafe. The strongest answer identifies the specific alliance component instead of concluding globally that the client is resistant, unmotivated, or a poor fit.",
